# Localisation

Library chrome is localised. Supported locales are **`en`** (default) and **`es`**. Do not hardcode English or Spanish in JSX.

Every new key must be added to **both** [`src/i18n/en.ts`](src/i18n/en.ts) and [`src/i18n/es.ts`](src/i18n/es.ts). Read copy with `t('key')` from `useT()`.

Host content (`value`, consumer `placeholder`) is the consuming app’s copy — the library does not translate it. Playground chrome uses `playground/src/i18n/`, not library dictionaries.

```tsx
// ❌ BAD — hardcoded chrome
<button aria-label="Editor mode">Visual</button>

// ✅ GOOD — dictionary key, both locales
<button aria-label={t('modeVisualAria')}>{t('modeVisual')}</button>
```
